						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=991.msg11300#msg11300"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=991.msg11300#msg11300">Re: Rodcet Nife Allstars</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #120 on:</b> September 20, 2004, 06:14:48 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							They&#039;re = Contraction for &#039;they are&#039;<br />Their = meaning posession; The possessive form of &#039;they&#039;.<br />There = (adverb) Representing a place/location<br />(pronoun) Used to introduce a sentence, i.e. &quot;There will be no dawn for Men.&quot;<br /><br />It&#039;s = Contraction for &#039;it is&#039;<br />Its = posession<br /><br />Two = The number 2<br />Too = including; in addition; an excessive amount of something<br />To = ...it means &#039;to&#039;...that is all.<br /><br />Here = location<br />Hear = To perceive sound by the ear; one of the five senses.<br /><br />Where = location<br />We&#039;re = we are<br />Were = past tense of &quot;are&quot;<br /><br />since = A word<br />sinse = Not a word<br /><br />sense = A word<br />sence = Not a word<br /><br />Lose - to fail, not win<br />Loose - not tight<br /><br />You&#039;re = you are<br />Your = posession<br />ur = A city of ancient Sumer in southern Mesopotamia on a site in present-day southeast Iraq. One of the oldest cities in Mesopotamia, it was an important center of Sumerian culture after c. 3000 b.c. and the birthplace of Abraham. The city declined after the sixth century B.C.
						</td>
					</tr>
